EXTRA_SCENARIOS=[
('I am afraid of disappointing my family','Decisions & change',18,'Separate love from agreement. Write what you can honestly promise. Explain your reasons calmly and ask for time to decide.','A student can respect a parent while asking to explore a different course before committing.','relationships'),
('Two people I love are fighting','Relationships',12,'Do not carry messages that increase anger. Listen separately, state what you can help with, and invite direct conversation when it is safe.','Tell each person you care about both and will help arrange a calm conversation, but will not pass insults.','relationships'),
('I cannot forgive myself','Confidence & setbacks',6,'Name the harm without calling your whole self bad. Repair what can be repaired. Choose a daily practice that makes repetition less likely.','An apology, repayment and a changed routine turn regret into responsibility.','promises'),
('I feel angry about unfair treatment','Relationships',3,'Record what happened and its effect. Choose a proportionate response: a clear conversation, written request, or help from someone responsible.','Document repeated exclusion from work and ask the manager for a specific role in the next experiment.','relationships'),
('I have to give difficult feedback','Relationships',17,'Describe one observed action and its effect. Ask for the other person’s view. Agree on one change and a time to review it.','“The report came after the decision” is more useful than “You are unreliable.”','relationships'),
('I am tempted to gossip','Habits & balance',16,'Pause before repeating it. Ask whether it is verified, necessary and kind. Speak directly to the person involved if action is needed.','Do not forward a rumour about a colleague’s mistake; ask them privately about the work.','promises'),
('I feel guilty when I rest','Habits & balance',6,'Treat rest as maintenance for your responsibilities. Decide its duration, protect it, and return to the next task without apology.','A planned evening walk and early sleep can support tomorrow’s work.','rest'),
('My phone controls my attention','Habits & balance',6,'Choose one phone-free place and one phone-free hour. Remove the strongest trigger and replace it with a visible activity.','Charge the phone outside the bedroom and keep the book or mat you want to use in sight.','learning'),
('I start many things and finish none','Learning & work',2,'Choose one outcome to finish this week. Put the other ideas on a later list. Define what “done” means before starting.','Finish and share one working prototype before adding another feature.','learning'),
('I am working hard but going nowhere','Learning & work',4,'Name the result you need, the evidence of progress and the next checkpoint. Stop work that does not serve that result.','Replace vague studying with twenty practice questions and a review of errors.','results'),
('I do not know when to quit','Decisions & change',18,'Set three tests: what improvement is still possible, what further effort costs, and what new evidence would change the decision. Choose a review date.','A project gets two more weeks to meet a measurable milestone before resources move elsewhere.','decisions'),
('I regret the time I already spent','Decisions & change',2,'Judge the next step by future cost and value. Keep the useful learning, but do not make past effort a reason to spend more.','Years spent learning a skill can remain valuable even if you change direction.','decisions'),
('Success is making me arrogant','Confidence & setbacks',10,'Name the people and conditions that helped. Keep one task that makes you a learner. Use part of your success to help someone else grow.','After a promotion, ask the team what support made the result possible and mentor a junior colleague.','self-worth'),
('I feel invisible at work or school','Confidence & setbacks',3,'Make your contribution concrete. Ask for ownership of a named task, share progress briefly, and request specific feedback.','Offer to own the next test plan and circulate a one-page result.','self-worth'),
('Someone takes credit for my work','Relationships',16,'Keep dated evidence. Correct the record calmly with the relevant person. State the contribution and the credit you expect next time.','Send the shared result with a clear list of who designed, measured and analysed it.','promises'),
('I must choose between safety and growth','Decisions & change',18,'Protect the minimum you cannot risk. Test the new path in a small reversible way. Decide using evidence from that test.','Try a part-time course or pilot project before leaving stable work.','decisions'),
('I feel jealous of a sibling','Relationships',12,'Name the need beneath the comparison. Ask for what you need directly and notice one strength that belongs to your own path.','Ask for time with a parent rather than attacking the attention given to a sibling.','relationships'),
('My child made a serious mistake','Care & connection',5,'Make safety and truth the first priorities. Hear the full account, set a proportionate consequence and include a repair.','A broken promise leads to replacing the loss and rebuilding trust through a clear routine.','promises'),
('An elder rejects my choice','Relationships',12,'Listen for the fear or value behind the objection. Explain your plan and safeguards. Keep respect while taking responsibility for your decision.','Share the finances and timeline behind a career choice instead of arguing only about freedom.','relationships'),
('I am caring for an ageing parent','Care & connection',3,'List medical, practical and emotional needs. Divide tasks by person and date. Protect the caregiver’s sleep and seek professional help when needed.','One relative handles appointments, another medicines, and a third weekly companionship.','helping'),
('I cannot concentrate while grieving','Care & connection',2,'Reduce expectations for a while. Keep food, sleep and one essential task. Ask someone trusted to help with decisions that can wait.','Complete one necessary form, then stop and rest rather than forcing a full workday.','rest'),
('I am anxious about money','Decisions & change',17,'Write the exact numbers: essential expenses, debt, savings and next income. Take one protective step and get qualified advice for major decisions.','Cancel one avoidable cost and schedule a review with a trusted financial professional.','uncertainty'),
('I must speak in front of people','Confidence & setbacks',6,'Prepare the first minute and three main points. Practise aloud once. Slow the first two sentences and look at one friendly face.','A clear opening and three examples matter more than memorising every word.','self-worth'),
('I have lost motivation for something I loved','Habits & balance',6,'Lower the entry cost. Return for ten minutes without demanding the old feeling. Notice whether rest, grief or a changed value needs attention.','Play one familiar song or take a short walk; let interest return through contact rather than pressure.','rest')]
